---
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
import "../style/pages/legal.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | ToolVector"
  description="Read ToolVector's Affiliate Disclosure to understand how we earn revenue, our affiliate relationships, and how they affect our content."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-page__hero">
      <div class="container legal-page__hero-inner">
        <div class="legal-page__badge">Legal</div>
        <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
        <p class="legal-page__meta">
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-07-30">July 30, 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-page__lead">
          We believe in transparency. This page explains how ToolVector earns
          revenue and how that relationship does (or does not) influence the
          content you read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container legal-page__body">
      <aside class="legal-toc">
        <p class="legal-toc__label">On this page</p>
        <nav>
          <a href="#commitment">1. Our Commitment to Transparency</a>
          <a href="#how-we-make-money">2. How ToolVector Makes Money</a>
          <a href="#effect-on-reviews">3. How This Affects Our Reviews</a>
          <a href="#review-process">4. Our Review Process</a>
          <a href="#identify-content">5. How to Identify Affiliate Content</a>
          <a href="#no-extra-cost">6. No Extra Cost to You</a>
          <a href="#questions">7. Questions or Feedback</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <article class="legal-content">
        <div class="legal-notice">
          <span class="legal-notice__icon">⚠️</span>
          <p>
            This is a suggested draft based on the features currently visible on
            the site. This is <strong>not legal advice</strong>. In some regions
            (e.g., the U.S. — FTC), the law requires affiliate disclosures to be
            clear and conspicuous — have this reviewed carefully before
            publishing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section id="commitment">
          <h2>1. Our Commitment to Transparency</h2>
          <p>
            ToolVector is a B2B software review and comparison platform. We
            believe in transparency, so this page explains how we earn revenue
            and how that relationship does (or does not) influence the content
            you read on ToolVector.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="how-we-make-money">
          <h2>2. How ToolVector Makes Money</h2>
          <p>ToolVector may earn compensation through the following:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Affiliate links</strong>: When you click a link on
              ToolVector (e.g., in a review, comparison table, or our <strong
                >Deals</strong
              > section) and subsequently sign up for or purchase a product from that
              vendor (e.g., Semrush, NordVPN, Notion, etc.), we may earn a commission
              from that vendor. This comes <strong
                >at no extra cost to you</strong
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Sponsored content / advertising</strong>: Some articles,
              banners, or placements on the site may be sponsored by a software
              vendor. Such content is always clearly labeled (e.g., "Sponsored,"
              "Ad").
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Listing fees</strong>: Some software vendors may pay a fee
              for enhanced or featured placement through our <strong
                >"List your tool"</strong
              > section or <strong>Advertise</strong> packages.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="effect-on-reviews">
          <h2>3. How This Affects Our Reviews</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Earning a commission or advertising fee <strong
                >does not change the actual opinion</strong
              > of the ToolVector team regarding a product's quality.
            </li>
            <li>
              For full transparency: tools with an affiliate relationship <strong
                >may be given greater visibility</strong
              > in certain lists, deal banners, or Smart Match recommendations — provided
              the product still meets our review criteria.
            </li>
            <li>
              We also review and list many products that have <strong>no</strong
              > affiliate relationship with ToolVector, in order to keep our categories
              and rankings objective.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="review-process">
          <h2>4. Our Review Process</h2>
          <p>Reviews, rankings, and comparisons on ToolVector are built on:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Research into features, pricing, and publicly available vendor
              documentation
            </li>
            <li>Hands-on testing (trials/demos) where possible</li>
            <li>Feedback and reviews from real users</li>
            <li>Comparison against similar products in the same category</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Regardless of any affiliate relationship, our team aims to evaluate
            products based on the real value they provide to users.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="identify-content">
          <h2>5. How to Identify Affiliate Content</h2>
          <p>
            You can recognize content that may contain affiliate links through:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Our <strong>Deals</strong> section (offers, discount codes)</li>
            <li>
              Buttons such as "Get Deal," "Try [Product]," or "Visit Website"
              within reviews
            </li>
            <li>
              "Sponsored" / "Ad" labels (where applicable) on articles or
              banners
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="no-extra-cost">
          <h2>6. No Extra Cost to You</h2>
          <p>
            Clicking an affiliate link on ToolVector <strong
              >does not increase</strong
            > the price you pay for a product or service — any commission we may receive
            is paid by the vendor out of their own revenue, not added to the price
            you see.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>7. Questions or Feedback</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about our affiliate relationship with any
            product mentioned on the site, or would like to report content you
            believe lacks proper transparency, please contact us:
          </p>
          <div class="legal-contact-card">
            <a href="mailto:yen@toolvector.io">
              <span>📧</span> yen@toolvector.io
            </a>
            <a href="/contact/">
              <span>🌐</span> toolvector.io/contact
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="legal-footer-note">
          This page should be read together with ToolVector's
          <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a> and
          <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
